==History==
2023
*The Super Ice Golem [[Cards|card]] was made available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Super Ice Golem Challenge]] on 9/1/2023.
*On 15/1/2023, the Super Ice Golem was removed from the game.
*On 10/4/2023, the Super Ice Golem was readded to the game in the Super Cards Triple Draft Event.
*On 18/4/2023, the Super Ice Golem was removed from the game.
2024
*On 19/8/2024, the Super Ice Golem was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 26/8/2024, the Super Ice Golem was removed from the game.
2025
*On 27/1/2025, the Super Ice Golem was readded to the game in the Super Cards Draft Event.
*On 3/2/2025, the Super Ice Golem was removed from the game.

==Trivia==
*The word "Golem" occurs once in the Bible in Psalm 139:16, which uses the word "''golmi''", that means "my light form", "raw" material, connoting the unfinished human being. A golem is an animated, anthropomorphic being in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_folklore Jewish folklore], which is entirely created from inanimate matter, usually clay or mud. The most famous golem narrative involves [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel Judah Loew ben Bezalel], the late 16th-century rabbi of Prague.
*The Super Ice Golem is 1 of 7 [[cards]] associated with ice, with the others being [[Ice Spirit]], [[Giant Snowball]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Freeze]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Wizard Trio]].
**In the Finnish language setting of the game, the Ice Golem's name translates to "Super Freezing Golem".
*The Super Ice Golem has the lowest speed of all [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]], with a speed of 30.
*Unlike the [[Golem]], the Super Ice Golem attacks with both hands, whereas the Golem only punches with one hand. The [[Elixir Golem]] attacks with both hands, but the Elixir Golemites use one hand and the Elixir Blobs appear to bite.
*Unlike the Golem and Elixir Golem, the Super Ice Golem doesn't spawn his smaller versions upon death.
*The description of the Super Ice Golem incorrectly states that he slows nearby troops upon death. This is because the description is copied from the Ice Golem.

